## Sprint goal

By the end of Sprint 2, a member of staff can do all of this on the live dev site, **https://crs-dev-i3q75k.azurewebsites.net**:

1. Register a walk-in customer, or find one who has been in before
2. Log a repair ticket for them
3. Assign the ticket to a technician
4. Move the ticket along its status (Diagnosing → Awaiting approval, and so on)
5. Find the ticket again in the ticket list using filters
6. Check parts stock, with low stock highlighted

This is the first half of the **Walk-in repair** flow on the UX Design page. Quotes, reserving parts and closing tickets come in Sprint 3.

