### What each layer does

This is the routes → controllers → services → data access structure from the Architecture page.

| Layer | File | Does | Never does |
|---|---|---|---|
| Route | `*.routes.js` | Connects a URL to a controller function | Any logic |
| Controller | `*.controller.js` | Reads the request, calls the service, sends the response | SQL or business rules |
| Service | `*.service.js` | Checks the input and applies the rules (for example, which status changes are allowed) | SQL, or touching `req`/`res` |
| Data access | `*.data.js` | Runs SQL queries, always with parameters | Validation, or touching `req`/`res` |

A worked example of all four layers is in the [Appendix](#appendix-pattern-to-copy). Copy it.

