### Every page follows these basics

These come from the usability notes on the UX Design page and the Security Considerations page.

- Status and priority badges show **text as well as colour** ("Repairing", not only an orange dot), so they work for colour-blind users and screen readers.
- Every input has a `<label>`.
- Anything clickable is a real `<button>` or `<a>`, so it works with the keyboard.
- If the API returns an error, show the message on the page, not only in the console.
- Show text that users typed with `textContent`, **never** `innerHTML` (this blocks script injection, the XSS risk on the Security page).
- Load everything through the shared `api.js` helper.

