## Security this sprint

These are the risks from the Security Considerations register that apply to code we write now.

| Risk | What we do in Sprint 2 |
|---|---|
| SQL injection | Every query passes values with `.input(...)`. Reviewers reject any pull request that builds SQL by joining strings with user input. |
| Script injection (XSS) | `textContent`, never `innerHTML`, for anything a user typed |
| Secrets committed to the repo | `.env` stays in `.gitignore`. The database password never goes in code, commits or this wiki. |
| Vulnerable third-party packages | `npm audit` step added to the pipeline as part of finishing #23 |
| Customer personal data exposed | HTTPS Only on the App Service (F6); only fake data on the dev site |

Sign-in, roles, password rules, the audit log and the key vault all depend on the #60 decision, so they wait for a later sprint (see [Future sprints](#future-sprints)).

